id: pm-rl-confined-sdk-locks
title: Provide descriptor-relative SDK lock acquisition before claiming state confinement
description: "Blocking Cubic thread PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRp3 reproduces a real check/use race in acquireStateLock. Replacing the locks directory with a symlink after statePath and before the native SDK mkdir writes the lock outside state. acquireStateLease and commitStateTransaction have the same SDK pathname boundary. The pinned SDK 2026.10.27 and inspected 2026.11.1 API expose no descriptor-relative lock/filesystem primitive. A second pathname check does not close the window; a private lease does not exclude ordinary writers. This is an unresolved P1 dependency, not an accepted deferral or completed fix."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: blocking,filesystem,"gh:unbraind/pm-rl#107",sdk-gap,"upstream:pm-cli#1647"
created_at: "2026-11-01T07:42:57.963Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-01T16:54:38.352Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Acquire, fence, release, stale cleanup owner writes and recovery audit writes operate through no-follow component handles, or refuse with a typed unsupported/boundary code before following an unsafe path.; Real filesystem regressions swap root, locks, cleanup gate and recovery directory at use; outside bytes and directory entries remain unchanged; ordinary roots and symlinked ancestors above the root retain released behavior.; Preserve native SDK token, stale-owner and fenced-lease semantics without a second hand-written lock protocol or process-global filesystem monkeypatch; regressions fail on revert."
parent: pm-rl-review107cubic
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-01T10:09:22.335Z",codex-agent,"Public API audit: node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli/dist/core/lock/lock.d.ts:109,118 expose acquireLock(pmRoot:string, id:string, ...) and acquireLockLease(pmRoot:string, id:string, ...), with no directory handle or filesystem capability parameter. sdk/workspace-transaction.d.ts:43-63 likewise accepts a string pmRoot and no filesystem provider. Native stale cleanup opens its owner path after awaited pathname operations. The latest inspected public SDK has the same limitation. Upstream issue search for symlink lock returned no matching open issue; no issue was filed. pm-cli#1620 concerns ordinary writers and is not evidence of path confinement. This dependency remains an unresolved blocking P1, not an approved scope deferral."
body: ""
